In `db.js:11-16`, `client.release()` runs only on the success path. If `fn(client)` throws, the connection is never returned to the pool and stays checked out. The log is consistent with that: `idle` stays at 0 and `waiting` climbs from 7 to 28 over about two and a half minutes. Slow queries holding connections would look the same, so the log alone can't rule them out. Either way, a leaked connection permanently shrinks the pool, so raising `max` only pushes the failure out.

The fix is to release in a `finally`:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

